# Keeps the build context (and therefore what could ever reach a build
# step) to what deploy/Dockerfile actually COPYs. In particular .env and
# .git must never be sent to a docker daemon -- see .gitignore's own
# "Secrets" block for why .env is never committed either.
.git/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/

# Everything under data/ except what deploy/Dockerfile explicitly COPYs
# (data/processed/, data/watch/, data/app/.gitkeep) -- no reason to send
# data/raw or data/historical into the build context at all.
data/*
!data/processed/
!data/watch/
!data/app/
data/app/*
!data/app/.gitkeep
# COLD-STORAGE ARCHIVE SHIPS IN THE IMAGE (2026-09-21 incident, src.
# pipeline.store_archive; corrected 2026-09-21 review -- an earlier version
# of this comment said the archive could be left out because the ONLY
# reader of odds_multibook.jsonl in the serving container is apphealth's
# check_store. That was false: it only grepped api/ itself, not what api/
# imports. At least seven served routes read odds_multibook's CONTENT
# through snapshots.read_multibook / iter_multibook / gamekey.
# events_for_date, all of which now read the LOGICAL store (hot + archive)
# via store_archive -- api/odds.py -> prices.boards_by_matchup,
# api/games.py -> engine_bridge.decisions_for_date, api/card.py ->
# report.card / report.nfl_card, api/tennis.py -> tennis_board, api/
# today.py -> gamekey.events_for_date. Every one of those takes an
# arbitrary `date` (the UI has a date picker and deep-links from past card
# picks, web/js/games.js, web/js/card.js), so leaving the archive out of
# the image would make every past-date /odds, /games, /card and /opportunities
# view go blank the moment a store rotation first fires -- a real,
# customer-facing regression from what the image served before this
# incident (the full, unrotated file). The archive is gzip and, for the
# rotation policy this project actually runs (3-day keep window), small: a
# multi-week segment compresses to a few MB, nowhere near the 100 MB hot
# file the image already shipped pre-incident. apphealth.check_store stays
# hot-file-only regardless (its own docstring) -- that was never the reason
# to exclude the archive, only a fact that happens to be true either way.
# data/processed/archive/  -- INTENTIONALLY NOT EXCLUDED, see above.
# Paper-account ledgers: read by the Performance surface (2026-09-07).
!data/paper_accounts/
# F-2 (2026-09-07): the historical stores the matchup page reads for team
# records, starter form, bullpen workload, posted lineups and handedness.
# They are git-ignored and live in the daily-loop actions/cache; the deploy
# workflow restores that cache before building so they are present here.
# Only these five files -- data/historical/statcast (pitch-level, ~40 MB)
# stays out of the image until something on a customer route reads it.
!data/historical/
data/historical/*
!data/historical/mlb_results.csv
!data/historical/mlb_results.manifest.json
!data/historical/pitcher_logs.jsonl
!data/historical/bullpen_log.jsonl
!data/historical/lineups.jsonl
!data/historical/handedness.json
# The per-matchup analysis stores (2026-09-08): league position, batter-vs-
# pitcher history, pitcher platoon splits and pitch arsenals. ~1.1 MB
# together -- the arsenal SUMMARY is 688 KB, which is a different and far
# smaller artifact than the 40 MB pitch-level data/historical/statcast/
# store that still stays out of the image.
!data/historical/standings.jsonl
!data/historical/matchup_history.jsonl
!data/historical/matchup_pairs.json
!data/historical/pitcher_splits.json
!data/historical/arsenals/
!data/historical/transactions.jsonl
# The research registry, and only it: GET /meta's hypothesis counts read
# this file, and without it the live demo said "0 pre-registered research
# ideas" (2026-09-12). Sweep artifacts under data/research/ stay out.
!data/research/
data/research/*
!data/research/alpha_registry.jsonl

design/
docs/
artifacts/
# evidence/ is COPYd now (Performance + Opportunities surfaces read the
# engine ledgers) -- see deploy/Dockerfile.
.claude/
